    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 10</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LIIII. Gif hwa binnan þam gemærum ures rices reaflác ⁊ niednæme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.3-2"/> dó, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.4-2"/> he ðone reaflac ⁊ geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.5-2"/> LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.6-2"/> scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LIIII. . . . ru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ures rices . . ., . . þone . . . . . . ll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LIIII. Gif hwa reaflac ⁊ nydnæme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.2"/> binnan þam gemærum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.3"/> ures rices gedo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.4"/>, agife he ðone reaflac ⁊ gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.5"/> LX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Be reaflace. Gyf hwa binnan ðam gemærum ures rices reaflac ⁊ nydnæme dó, agyfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.1"/> he ðone reaflác ⁊ gesylle syxti scill' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis intra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.6"/> commarciones<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.7"/> (fines) regni nostri robariam et uiolentam captionem faciat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.8"/>, reddat ipsam robariam (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.9"/> persoluat) et emendet LX sol.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.10"/> pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_10.lnote.oe.11"/> wita.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be reaflac.] Gif hwa binnan þam gemærum ures rices reaflác ⁊ niednæme dó<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_10.attnote.fn.1"/>, agife he ðone reaflac ⁊ geselle LX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="10" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="376" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LIIII} Gif hwa binnan þam gemærum ures rices reaflác ⁊ niednæme dó, agife he ðone reaflac ⁊ geselle LX sciƚƚ to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand innerhalb der Grenzen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_10.lnote.de.1"/> unseres Reiches Raub<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_10.lnote.de.2"/> und gewaltsame<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_10.lnote.de.3"/> Wegnahme verübt, gebe er den Raub zurück<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_10.lnote.de.4"/> und zahle [dem König] 60 Schill. zur Strafe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone commits robbery and forcible seizure within the borders of our kingdom, let him give back the plunder and pay [the king] 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone within the borders of our kingdom commits an act of robbery or seizes anything with violence, he shall restore the plunder and pay a fine of 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone within the boundaries of our kingdom commit robbery and rapine, he is to give back the plunder and give 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="377" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone within the boundaries of our kingdom commits robbery and forceful plunder, let him return the plunder and give 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="376"><label>same term</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_39">VI Atr 39</ref> <quote>The term occurs in later legislation (as nydnæme) only in vi Æthelred §39 and ii Cnut §§52–52.1.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="376"><label>same term</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_52">II Cn 52–52.1</ref> <quote>The term occurs in later legislation (as nydnæme) only in vi Æthelred §39 and ii Cnut §§52–52.1.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="377"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_19">Abt 19</ref> <quote>Ine, as do the laws of the Continent, distinguishes between simple theft and robbery involving force. Compare Æthelberht §23.1 [L19].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><ref target="clause:Af_9-2">Af 9.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="305"><ref target="clause:IIAs_1">II As 1–1.5</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inter <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inter R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> f. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> co. [commer. <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi>] <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only f. Lond; only co. [commer. MHk] the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">perpetret <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">perpetret Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et p. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et p. lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wite <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> pro w. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wite instead of pro w. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">und</hi> æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y and æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">do <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur, folgt Rasur von etwa fünf Buchst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">do on an erasure, followed by an erasure of about five letters</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nydn. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nydn. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agyfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agyfe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">commarcio,</hi> verderbt aus mlat. <hi rend="italic">commarchia</hi> bei Ducange? — Ines Stil atmet hier sein persönliches oder des Königtums Machtbewusstsein; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Einl. 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">commarcio,</hi> corrupted from Med. Lat. <hi rend="italic">commarchia</hi> in Ducange? — Ine’s style here breathes his own sense of power, or that of the kingship; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Introduction 18</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Raub’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1. 4b) steht hier für ‘Rauben’ und 2 Z. nachher für ‘Geraubtes’; es gilt Agsä. auch von Land (<hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 4b)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Robbery’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1. 4b) stands here for ‘robbing’ and 2 ll. later for ‘what has been robbed’; in A.-S. it applies to land too (<hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 4b)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Den Unterschied von Raub und gewaltsamem Fortnehmen kennen auch andere Germanen; Brunner II 647; Richthofen in <hi rend="italic">Mon. Germ., Leg.</hi> III 664</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Other Germanic peoples too know the distinction between robbery and forcible taking; Brunner II 647; Richthofen in <hi rend="italic">Mon. Germ., Leg.</hi> III 664</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_10.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Busse ist hier (gegen <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 9³) nicht erwähnt (erst von Q spät. Rez., gemäss späterem Rechte eingesetzt), dagegen das Strafgeld verdoppelt, wie für Diebstahl; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Compensation is not mentioned here (in contrast to <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 9³) (it was inserted only by Q’s later recension, in accordance with later law), whereas the fine is doubled, as for theft; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 19</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_10.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>dó</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Gif hwa reaflac ⁊ nydnæme binnan…rices gedo</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
